                <pb facs="0477" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/23394: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Second Secretary of
                        Legation in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thompson</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Temporarily in France</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-08-19T21:00:00-04:00">August 19, 1942—9
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>512. Your 1160, August 7, midnight. In your discretion, support Dr. Lowrie’s
                    application to the Marshal to extend for the present the residence permits of
                    those Jews whose documentation to emigrate from France is nearly complete.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
